Q: Synchronously immediately resolved promise behaviour when passed as argument? A: <p>Promises go into <a href="https://javascript.info/microtask-queue#microtasks-queue" rel="nofollow noreferrer">the microtask queue</a>, that is consumed once all other operations are done.</p>
<p>It works with a single promise too:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const promise = Promise.resolve(1);
promise.then(console.log);
console.log(2);
</code></pre>
<p>The code above logs <code>2, 1</code>.</p>

Q: Why does C++ conversion from double to float show digits after 8th decimal place? A: <p>After the number of significant decimal digits, the trailing digits lose precision fidelity.</p>
<p>You can see it more clearly if you print out the entire representation (here are the routines I use):</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>static auto to_decimal_text(double d) -&gt; string {
    std::ostringstream ss;
    ss &lt;&lt; std::setfill('0') &lt;&lt; std::setprecision(2048) &lt;&lt; std::fixed &lt;&lt; d;
    auto result{ ss.str() };

    while(result.size() &gt; 2 &amp;&amp; result.back() == '0') {
        result.pop_back();
        if (result.back() == '.') {
            result.push_back('0');
            break;
        }
    }

    return result;
}

static auto to_decimal_text(float f) -&gt; string {
    std::ostringstream ss;
    ss &lt;&lt; std::setfill('0') &lt;&lt; std::setprecision(2048) &lt;&lt; std::fixed &lt;&lt; f;
    auto result{ ss.str() };

    while(result.size() &gt; 2 &amp;&amp; result.back() == '0') {
        result.pop_back();
        if (result.back() == '.') {
            result.push_back('0');
            break;
        }
    }

    return result;
}
</code></pre>
<p>The routines are not terribly performant.  I use them only for diagnostics.</p>
<p>The numbers will make more sense if you print them as hexadecimal floating point, or as binary floating point.  Then you will see the differences in the ULPs.</p>
